"# Walkthrough – Visual Object Gizmo Refinements & AI Diffusion Generation\n\nWe have resolved all 4 visual object interaction and generation issues in the **Aesthetic Compiler Studio**:\n\n1. **Delete Button Fixed (`🗑️ Delete`)**:\n   - **Issue**: Clicking Delete did not remove the object because `deselectVisualObject(doc)` cleared `activeVisualObject` before `remove()` was called.\n   - **Fix**: Cached the element reference (`const target = activeVisualObject;`) prior to deselecting, ensuring both the DOM element and its active gizmo are cleanly deleted.\n2. **Real AI Image Generation (Fixing the Static Flower Photo)**:\n   - **Issue**: The AI image prompt was returning a hardcoded Unsplash flower photo on every prompt.\n   - **Fix**: Integrated dynamic AI diffusion image generation (`https://image.pollinations.ai/prompt/{prompt}?width=800&height=800&nologo=true&seed={seed}`) in both `server.py` and client-side `studio/ai.js`. Every prompt produces a unique, high-resolution graphic matching the user's prompt (e.g., prompt for `\"cyberpunk skull stamp\"` produces a real skull stamp).\n3. **Ergonomic Rotate Handle Separation**:\n   - **Issue**: The rotate glyph sat directly underneath the gizmo menu pill, making it impossible to click or drag without clicking a menu button.\n   - **Fix**: Separated vertical layers:\n     - Rotate stem & handle positioned at `top: -26px` and `top: -38px`.\n     - Action toolbar positioned at `top: -82px`, providing **44px of vertical clearance**.\n     - Auto-flip detection: If an element is within 95px of the sheet top, `.vo-toolbar-bottom` dynamically flips the toolbar below the object (`top: calc(100% + 20px)`).\n4. **Clean Figma-Style Resize Handle**:\n   - **Issue**: The resize handle rendered an awkward static unicode arrow `⤡` inside a dark colorblock.\n   - **Fix**: Removed the text character glyph completely. Replaced with an industry-standard 10×10px white square anchor with a crisp 2px primary blue border, subtle drop shadow, and `nwse-resize` cursor.\n\n---\n
